1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,787
Why Multitasking Does Not Work.

2
00:00:02,737 --> 00:00:07,200
The brain cannot focus on two cognitive tasks simultaneously.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,425
What is called multitasking is actually rapid task-switching.

4
00:00:11,425 --> 00:00:14,925
Each switch incurs a cost in time and accuracy.

5
00:00:14,925 --> 00:00:23,762
Studies by Earl Miller at MIT show that heavy multitaskers perform worse on attention and memory tests than those who focus on one thing at a time.

6
00:00:23,762 --> 00:00:28,387
For tasks requiring thought, single-tasking is far more efficient.

7
00:00:28,387 --> 00:00:36,000
Turning off notifications, closing extra tabs, and giving one task undivided attention produces better results.

